<Copy k="widget.description">
  Diagram: four stacked layers of access, titled Access compounds, with models
  as the widest layer at the base. Models are which models people can reach
  and how capable they are. Harnesses are the scaffolding around the model,
  such as agents and tool permissions. Surfaces are where AI shows up: chat,
  developer tools, and the apps people already work in. Features, at the top,
  are what's switched on, such as memory, projects, and connections to your
  data. The lesson says each layer complements the rest, that access is the
  lever an organization controls most directly, and that mindsets and skills
  can't compensate for missing access.
</Copy>
